      "rationale": "Three critical concurrent papers are entirely missing from the landscape: UserRL (arXiv:2509.19736, Sep 2025) already applies GRPO on TauGym (a τ-bench gym) with LLM-simulated users and explicitly includes IntentionGym for training clarification on underspecified tasks using Qwen3 models — this is near-identical to the core proposal; SpeakRL (arXiv:2512.13159, Dec 2025) uses GRPO with verifiable rewards to train clarification question-asking on underspecified multi-turn dialogue and achieves a 20% task-completion improvement; MUA-RL (arXiv:2508.18669, Aug 2025) integrates LLM-simulated users into the RL loop for agentic tool use and evaluates on TAU2 airline/retail/telecom. After accounting for these papers, the only genuinely novel element is the LHAW dimension-targeting secondary reward — a thin differentiation insufficient to anchor an EMNLP 2026 main track submission."
