    "feasibility": {
      "score": 2,
      "rationale": "Three independent feasibility blockers: (1) LHAW's released data covers TheAgentCompany, SWE-Bench Pro, and MCP-Atlas only — applying the full LHAW pipeline (segment extraction → candidate generation → empirical agent trials for outcome-criticality classification) to τ-bench from scratch likely requires 2–4 weeks of engineering alone, well outside the 16-day window; (2) The proposal reports only A100 hours without converting to H100: manual mode (~400h A100 ≈ 200–267h H100) is borderline, human-in-loop (~550h A100 ≈ 275–367h H100) and auto-research (~900h A100 ≈ 450–600h H100) both violate the stated ≤200 H100-hour hard constraint; (3) GRPO training with 2,000 variants × 8+ rollouts each requires ~160k–480k LLM API calls to the τ-bench user simulator per training pass, implying $8k–$24k+ in API costs per pass that are entirely absent from the resource estimate."
