      "rationale": "The CLARITI differentiation argument (short τ-bench episodes make binary task-success tractable as a GRPO signal) is well-articulated and technically sound; however, the landscape section has a critical gap — UserRL, SpeakRL, and MUA-RL are all omitted, which a reviewer will immediately flag, and the 'no existing work couples X with Y' claim is demonstrably false after those papers. The resource estimates are internally inconsistent (A100 vs. H100 units, auto-mode timeline is unrealistic for the stated parallel-GPU count given user-simulator serialization bottleneck)."
